            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "soap (MED s.v. sope n. (2)) | a wooden case in which soap is packed (OED s.v. soap-box) | ball-soap, commonly used in the North, made with lyes from ashes and tallow (OED s.v. soap 2a, quote 1728) | ashes of certain kinds of wood used in forming a lye in soap-making (OED s.v. soap-ashes) | Castle soape manufactured in Castile, a fine hard soap prepared with olive oil and soda (OED s.v. Castile soap); Venice soape manufactured in Venice | made in Flanders | white soap" ;
